PROMPT - set the prompt››Syntax:› PROMPT [text]››Sets the command prompt; PROMPT alone›shows it. These codes in the text are›replaced:› $L  drive letter and colon (A:)› $N  drive number and colon (1:)› $P  path of the current directory› $D  date› $T  time› $R  new line›An _ shows as a space.››PROMPT x is the same as SET PROMPT=x.›The default is D$N. With no $PROMPT at›all the prompt is >. $P reads the disk›each time the prompt is shown.››Examples:› PROMPT $L$P\› PROMPT $D_$L››See also: SET, PATH›